geelkii-yaraa	Geelkii yaraa	The Little Camel	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Subax wanaagsan oo qorraxdu diirran tahay, geel yar oo la yiraahdo Dalmar ayaa ku toosay miyiga. Dalmar wuxuu lahaa dhogor jilicsan oo bunni dahabi ah iyo indho waaweyn oo aad ula yaaban adduunka. Hooyadiis, oo ahayd hal weyn oo xasilloon, ayaa ku tiri: "Maanta waxaan u soconnaa ceelka biyaha macaan." Dalmar aad ayuu u farxay, lugihiisa dhaadheer ayuuna ku boodbooday ciidda cas. Jidka dhexdiisa, wuxuu ku arkay shimbir yar oo ku heesaysa geedka quraca korkiisa. "Nabad, shimbir yahay!" ayuu yiri geelkii yaraa. "Ma taqaannaa halka uu ku yaallo ceelka biyaha?" Shimbirtii waxay u tilmaamtay dhinaca buurta cagaaran, halkaas oo neecaw qabow ka imaanaysay. Markii uu Dalmar daalay, hooyadiis ayaa uga sheekaysay sida geelu ugu adkaysto safarka dheer. Ugu dambayntii, waxay gaareen ceelkii, Dalmarna wuxuu cabbay biyo qabow oo nadiif ah. Fiidkii markii xiddiguhu soo baxeen, geelkii yaraa wuxuu ku seexday hooyadiis agteeda isagoo dhoolla-caddaynaya.	On a bright morning when the sun was warm, a little camel named Dalmar woke up in the countryside. Dalmar had soft golden-brown fur and big eyes that wondered eagerly at the world. His mother, who was a tall and calm she-camel, said to him: "Today we are walking to the well of sweet water." Dalmar was very happy, and with his long legs he skipped playfully across the red sand. Along the path, he saw a little bird singing on top of the umbrella thorn acacia tree. "Peace, little bird!" said the little camel. "Do you know where the water well is located?" The bird pointed toward the green hill, where a cool breeze was blowing from. When Dalmar grew tired, his mother told him stories about how camels endure the long journey. Finally, they reached the well, and Dalmar drank cool, clean water. In the evening when the stars came out, the little camel fell asleep beside his mother while smiling.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	xayawaanka	1	40
shimbirtii-iyo-roobka	Shimbirtii Yaraa iyo Roobka Gu’ga	The Little Bird and the Spring Rain	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Shimbir yar oo la yiraahdo Canab ayaa ku noolayd geedka quraca korkiisa. Subax walba waxay eegi jirtay daruuraha cadcad ee cirka maraya. Maalin maalmaha ka mid ah, neecaw qabow ayaa soo dhacday, roobka gu’ga ayaana bilowday. Dhibcaha roobka ayaa ku dhacay caleemaha geedaha iyo ciidda miyiga. Geedaha iyo ubaxyada miyiga ayaa isla markiiba noqday kuwo cagaaran oo qurux badan. Shimbirtii yaraa waxay qaadday hees farxad leh oo ay ku soo dhawaynayso biyaha macaan.	A little bird named Canab lived at the top of the umbrella thorn acacia tree. Every morning she used to look up at the white clouds moving across the sky. One day, a cool breeze blew across the land, and the spring rain began to fall. Raindrops fell softly onto the tree leaves and the countryside soil. The trees and wildflowers of the countryside soon turned green and beautiful. The little bird sang a joyful song welcoming the sweet rain water.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	dabeecadda	2	40
bisaddii-baroor	Bisaddii Yarayd ee Baroor	Baroor the Little Kitten	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Guriga reer Axmed waxaa joogta bisad yar oo la yiraahdo Baroor. Baroor waxay leedahay dhogor cad iyo baro bunni ah oo qurux badan. Subaxdii waxay ku dhawaaqdaa "Miyaw, miyaw!" iyadoo raadinaysa Sahra. Sahra oo ah gabadh yar ayaa dhiisha ka soo shubtay caano diirran. Bisaddii yaraa waxay cabtay caanihii, ka dibna kubbad yar ayay ku ciyaartay. Markii ay daashay, waxay ku dul seexatay dermada hooska geedka.	At the Axmed family home lives a little cat named Baroor. Baroor has white fur with beautiful brown spots. In the morning she calls out "Meow, meow!" while looking for Sahra. Sahra, a young girl, poured warm milk from the traditional milk vessel. The little cat drank the milk, and afterward played with a small ball. When she grew tired, she curled up to sleep on the woven mat in the tree shade.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	xayawaanka	3	40
riyo-yar-oo-geesi-ah	Ri’dii Yarayd ee Biciid	The Brave Little Kid Goat	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Miyiga cagaaran waxaa ku nool ri’ yar oo cad oo aad u firfircoon. Ri’da yari waxay jeceshahay inay ku booddo dhagaxaanta buurta. Subaxdii, adhiga oo dhan ayaa u baxay daaqa cawska cusub. Ri’dii yarayd waxay aragtay caleemo macaan oo ku yaalla geed gaaban. Waxay u yeertay riyaha kale si ay u wada cunaan caleemaha cagaaran. Galabtii, adhigii oo dheregsan ayaa si nabad ah ugu soo laabtay xerada.	In the green countryside lives a small white kid goat who is very lively. The little goat loves to jump across the rocks on the hill. In the morning, the whole flock went out to graze on the fresh grass. The little goat saw sweet leaves growing on a low bush. She called the other goats so they could eat the green leaves together. In the afternoon, the well-fed flock returned safely to the corral.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	xayawaanka	4	40
qorraxda-subaxdii	Qorraxda Subaxdii iyo Rooble	The Morning Sun and Little Rooble	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Qorraxda dahabiga ah ayaa subaxdii ka soo iftiintay daaqadda guriga. Rooble oo ah wiil yar ayaa sariirta ka kacay isagoo dhoolla-caddaynaya. Wuxuu ku dhaqday wejigiisa iyo gacmihiisa biyo nadiif ah. Hooyo iyo Aabbe ayuu ku yiri: "Subax wanaagsan!" Qoysku wuxuu wada cunay quraac macaan oo ah canjeero iyo caano. Ka dib, Rooble wuxuu diyaar u noqday inuu ciyaaro oo wax barto.	The golden sun shone brightly through the house window in the morning. Rooble, a young boy, got up from his bed while smiling. He washed his face and hands with clean water. He said to his mother and father: "Good morning!" The family ate a delicious breakfast of canjeero flatbread and milk together. Afterward, Rooble was ready to play and learn new things.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	qoyska	5	40
buuggii-cagaarnaa	Buuggii Cagaarnaa ee Hodan	Hodan’s Green Storybook	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Hodan waxay leedahay buug cusub oo midabkiisu yahay cagaar. Bogga koowaad waxay ku aragtay sawirka geel weyn iyo geed quraac ah. Bogga labaad waxaa ku sawiran shimbir buluug ah iyo qorrax huruud ah. Walaalkeed Cali ayaa la fariistay si ay u wada akhriyaan erayada. Hodan waxay farta ku fiiqday xarafka "B" oo ku qoran sabuuradda. Markii ay dhammeeyeen akhriska, Hodan waxay si taxaddar leh buuggii u gelisay boorsadeeda.	Hodan has a new book whose colour is green. On the first page she saw a picture of a tall camel and an acacia tree. On the second page are drawn a blue bird and a yellow sun. Her brother Cali sat down with her so they could read the words together. Hodan pointed with her finger at the letter "B" written on the slate. When they finished reading, Hodan carefully placed the book into her bag.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	dugsiga	6	40
xiddigaha-habeenkii	Xiddigaha Habeenkii iyo Dayaxa	The Night Stars and the Moon	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Markii qorraxdu dhacday, cirku wuxuu noqday mid deggen oo madow. Dayax nuuraya iyo xiddigo badan ayaa cirka ka soo muuqday. Warsame iyo aabbihiis waxay ku fariisteen dermo taal aqalka hortiisa. "Hal, labo, saddex, afar, shan!" Warsame ayaa farta ku tiriyay xiddigaha. Neecaw qabow oo udgoon ayaa ka soo dhacday dhanka geedaha. Warsame indhihiisii way cuslaadeen, wuxuuna ku seexday nabad iyo riyo macaan.	When the sun set, the sky became calm and dark. A glowing moon and many stars appeared in the sky. Warsame and his father sat on a woven mat in front of the traditional home. "One, two, three, four, five!" Warsame counted the stars with his finger. A cool, fragrant breeze blew gently from the direction of the trees. Warsame’s eyes grew sleepy, and he fell asleep in peace and sweet dreams.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	habeenkii	7	40
kalluunkii-dahabiga	Kalluunkii Dahabiga ahaa ee Badda	The Golden Fish of the Sea	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Badda buluugga ah ee xeebta waxaa ku nool kalluun yar oo midab dahabi ah leh. Kalluunku wuxuu jecel yahay inuu ku dhex dabaasho dhagaxaanta shacaabiga. Subaxdii, ilayska qorraxda ayaa biyaha badda ka dhigay sidii muraayad dhalaalaysa. Kalluunkii yaraa wuxuu kor u eegay doon alwaax ah oo shiraac cad leh. Carruur saaran doonta ayaa u gacan haatisay kalluunkii quruxda badnaa. Kalluunkii wuxuu ku laabtay saaxiibbadiis isagoo ku faraxsan badda nadiifka ah.	In the blue sea along the coast lives a little fish with a golden colour. The fish loves to swim among the colourful coral reef stones. In the morning, the sunlight made the sea water sparkle like a shining mirror. The little fish looked up at a wooden sailboat with a white sail. Children aboard the boat waved happily at the beautiful fish. The fish returned to his friends feeling happy in the clean sea.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	tacabur	8	40
ubaxii-beerteenna	Ubaxii Yaraa ee Beerteenna	The Little Flower in Our Garden	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Maryan waxay ciidda beerta ku aastay iniin yar. Subax walba waxay ku shubi jirtay biyo qabow. Qorraxda diirran ayaa iyaduna u iftiimisay beerta. Toddobaad ka dib, caleen yar oo cagaaran ayaa ciidda ka soo baxday. Dhawaan waxaa furmay ubax guduudan oo aad u udgoon. Shimbiraha iyo balanbaallista ayaa u yimid inay eegaan ubaxa Maryan.	Maryan planted a tiny seed in the garden soil. Every morning she poured cool water over it. The warm sun also shone down upon the garden. After a week, a tiny green leaf sprouted from the soil. Soon a fragrant red flower blossomed open. Birds and butterflies came to admire Maryan’s flower.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	dabeecadda	9	40
salaanta-wanaagsan	Salaanta Wanaagsan ee Samatar	Samatar’s Kind Greeting	Ages 3–5 • Da’da 3–5 sano	Level 1 — Bilowga (Ages 3–5)	Samatar waa wiil yar oo jecel dadka deriska ah iyo saaxiibbadiis. Markii uu arko waayeelka, wuxuu ku yiraahdaa: "Assalaamu Calaykum, awoowe!" Awoowe wuxuu ugu jawaabaa dhoolla-caddayn iyo duco wanaagsan. Garoonka ciyaarta wuxuu kula kulmay saaxiibkiis Liibaan. "Ma nabad baa, saaxiib?" ayuu weydiiyay Samatar isagoo faraxsan. "Waa nabad iyo barwaaqo!" ayuu ku jawaabay Liibaan, wayna wada ciyaareen.	Samatar is a young boy who loves his neighbours and his friends. When he sees an elder, he says: "Peace be upon you, grandfather!" Grandfather replies with a warm smile and a kind blessing. At the playground he met his friend Liibaan. "Is there peace, my friend?" asked Samatar happily. "It is peace and prosperity!" answered Liibaan, and they played together.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-1	saaxiibtinimada	10	40
qoyska-caasha	Qoyska Caasha iyo Galabtii Sheekada	Caasha’s Family and Story Afternoon	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Maalin kasta oo Jimce ah, qoyska Caasha waxay ku kulmaan barxadda weyn ee gurigooda. Caasha iyo walaalkeed Fu’aad waxay fidiyaan dermo midabbo badan leh oo lagu fariisto. Hooyo waxay diyaarisaa shaah udgoon oo qorfe iyo heyl lagu daray, carruurtana caano ayay u shubtaa. Ayeeyo Cambaro waxay soo qaaddaa buug weyn oo ay ku qoran yihiin sheekooyin iyo maahmaahyo Soomaaliyeed. Caasha ayaa cod dheer ku akhrisa cutubka koowaad, qoyska oo dhanna si aamusnaan leh ayuu u dhageystaa. Aabbe wuxuu carruurta weydiiyaa macnaha erayada cusub ee ay ka barteen sheekada. Galabtaasi waxay ku dhammaataa qosol, wada-sheekaysi, iyo jacayl qoys oo diirran.	Every Friday, Caasha’s family gathers in the spacious courtyard of their home. Caasha and her brother Fu’aad spread out a colourful woven mat to sit upon. Mother prepares fragrant tea spiced with cinnamon and cardamom, and pours milk for the children. Grandmother Cambaro brings a large book filled with Somali stories and proverbs. Caasha reads the first chapter aloud, and the whole family listens attentively. Father asks the children the meanings of the new words they learned from the story. That afternoon ends with laughter, conversation, and warm family love.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	qoyska	11	50
maalintii-koowaad-dugsiga	Maalintii Koowaad ee Dugsiga	The First Day of School	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Guuleed wuxuu xirtay dharkiisii nadiifka ahaa ee dugsiga, boorsadiisana wuxuu ku ritay buug iyo qalin. Markii uu gaaray albaabka fasalka, yara xishood ayaa galay sababtoo ah ardayda ma uusan aqoon. Macallin Xasan ayaa u dhoolla-caddeeyay oo ku yiri: "Soo dhawoow, Guuleed! Halkan soo fariiso." Wiil la yiraahdo Sharmaarke oo kursiga xiga fadhiyay ayaa la wadaagay qalinkiisa midabka leh. Macallinku wuxuu sabuuradda ku qoray xarfaha Af-Soomaaliga, ardayduna si farxad leh ayay ugu dhawaaqeen. Guuleed wuxuu sabuuradda ku qoray magaciisa, fasalka oo dhanna sacab ayuu u tumay. Duhurkii markii uu guriga ku noqday, wuxuu hooyadiis u sheegay inuu aad u jeclaaday dugsiga.	Guuleed put on his clean school uniform and packed a notebook and pencil into his bag. When he reached the classroom door, he felt a little shy because he did not know the students yet. Teacher Xasan smiled at him and said: "Welcome, Guuleed! Come sit right here." A boy named Sharmaarke sitting at the next desk shared his coloured pencils with him. The teacher wrote the Somali alphabet letters on the board, and the students pronounced them joyfully. Guuleed wrote his own name on the chalkboard, and the whole class applauded for him. At noon when he returned home, he told his mother that he loved school very much.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	dugsiga	12	50
laba-saaxiib-iyo-geedka	Laba Saaxiib iyo Geedka Haracsan	Two Friends and the Shady Tree	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Fartuun iyo Leyla waa laba saaxiib oo ku wada barbaarray isku xaafad. Maalin kulul ayay arkeen in barxadda ciyaarta aysan lahayn geed hoos laga harsado. Waxay go’aansadeen inay wada beeraan geed talaal ah oo weynaada. Fartuun waxay keentay baaldi biyo ah, Leylana waxay geedka ku wareejisay ood yar oo ka ilaalisa riyaha. Maalin kasta dugsiga ka dib, labada saaxiib way soo booqan jireen geedkooda. Sannad ka dib, geedkii wuxuu yeeshay laamo ballaaran oo carruurta xaafaddu hoos fariistaan.	Fartuun and Leyla are two close friends who grew up in the same neighbourhood. On a hot day they noticed that the playground had no tree to provide cool shade. They decided to plant a young sapling together that would grow tall. Fartuun brought a bucket of water, and Leyla built a small protective fence around the tree to keep goats away. Every day after school, the two friends visited and cared for their tree. A year later, the tree had wide leafy branches where the neighbourhood children sat in the shade.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	saaxiibtinimada	13	50
suuqa-khudaarta	Suuqa Khudaarta iyo Xisaabta	The Vegetable Market and Counting	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Subaxdii Sabtida, Cumar wuxuu qaaday dambiil weyn oo caws ka samaysan wuxuuna raacay hooyadiis. Suuqa khudaarta wuxuu ahaa mid cammiran oo ay yaallaan miro midabbo kala duwan leh. Hooyo waxay dooratay afar cambe oo bisil iyo lix moos oo huruud ah. "Cumarow, isugeynta afarta cambe iyo lixda moos waa imisa?" ayay weydiisay hooyadiis. "Afar lagu daray lix waa toban mirood, hooyo!" ayuu Cumar si kalsooni leh ugu jawaabay. Guriga ayay ku soo laabteen iyagoo sida khudaar cusub oo qoyska oo dhan ku filan.	On Saturday morning, Cumar picked up a large woven straw basket and went with his mother. The fruit and vegetable market was lively and filled with produce of many colours. Mother selected four ripe mangoes and six yellow bananas. "Cumar, what is the sum of the four mangoes and the six bananas?" asked his mother. "Four plus six is ten fruits, Mother!" Cumar answered confidently. They returned home carrying fresh produce enough for the whole family.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	qoyska	14	50
diinkii-xigmadda-lahaa	Diinkii Xigmadda Lahaa iyo Jiilaalka	The Wise Tortoise and the Dry Season	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Xilligii jiilaalka, balliyadii yaryaraa ee miyiga way gureen, xayawaankiina biyo ayay raadiyeen. Bakaylihii iyo dhurwaagii meel walba way u carareen iyagoo aan waxba ka fekerin. Diinkii duqa ahaa ee xigmadda lahaa wuxuu si deggen u xusuustay il-biyood qadiimi ah. "I soo raaca, oo talaabo xasilloon ku socda," ayuu diinkii ku yiri xayawaankii. Talaabo-talaabo ayuu uga hor kacay ilaa ay gaareen hooska dhagax weyn oo biyo qabow ka burqanayaan. Xayawaankii oo dhan waxay u mahadceliyeen diinkii xigmadda iyo samirka badnaa.	During the dry season, the small countryside ponds dried up, and the animals searched for water. The hare and the hyena ran in every direction without thinking carefully. The wise old tortoise calmly remembered an ancient natural spring. "Follow me, and walk with steady steps," the tortoise said to the animals. Step by step he led them until they reached the shade of a great boulder where cool water bubbled forth. All the animals thanked the tortoise for his wisdom and patience.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	xayawaanka	15	50
doonta-xeebta-berbera	Doonta Cad ee Xeebta Berbera	The White Sailboat on the Berbera Coast	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Subax jimce ah, Jamaal iyo aabbihiis waxay u lugeeyeen xeebta bacaadka cad ee Berbera. Dabaysha badda ayaa si macaan u soo dhacaysay, hirarkuna xeebta ayay ku soo jabayeen. Jamaal wuxuu farta ku fiiqay doon weyn oo alwaax ah oo shiraaceeda cad dabayshu buuxisay. "Aabbe, sidee ayay doontu u socotaa iyadoo aan matoor lahayn?" ayuu weydiiyay Jamaal. Aabbihiis ayaa u sharxay in shiraaca cad uu qabto xoogga dabaysha, taasina ay doonta hore u riixdo. Kalluumaysatadii doonta saarnaa ayaa xeebta ku soo xirtay iyagoo wada kalluun cusub. Jamaal wuxuu ku riyooday inuu maalin uun noqdo badmaax yaqaanna jihooyinka badda.	On a Friday morning, Jamaal and his father walked along the white sandy beach of Berbera. The sea breeze blew pleasantly, and the gentle waves rolled onto the shore. Jamaal pointed at a large wooden boat whose white sail was filled by the wind. "Father, how does the boat move without an engine?" asked Jamaal. His father explained that the white sail catches the power of the wind, which pushes the boat forward. The fishermen aboard the boat docked at the shore bringing fresh fish. Jamaal dreamed of one day becoming a navigator who knows the directions of the sea.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	tacabur	16	50
roobkii-la-sugayay	Roobkii La Sugayay ee Tuulada	The Long-Awaited Village Rain	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Daruuro waaweyn oo biyo sida ayaa galabtii isku gadaamay cirka tuulada. Hani iyo walaalaheed waxay nadiifiyeen mareegta biyaha u leexisa berkedda guriga. Daqiiqado ka dib, roob mahiigaan ah oo qabow ayaa si xoog leh u da’ay. Berkeddii biyaha ayaa buuxsantay, dhirtii oommanaydna caleemaheeda ayaa soo noolaaday. Riyihii iyo geeliiba waxay heleen biyo badan iyo caws cusub oo soo biqilay. Qoysaska tuulada oo dhan waxay ku farxeen barwaaqada iyo nimcada roobka.	Large rain-bearing clouds gathered across the village sky in the afternoon. Hani and her siblings cleaned the channel that directs rainwater into the home cistern. Minutes later, a cool, abundant rain began to fall steadily. The water cistern filled up, and the thirsty plants revived their green leaves. Both the goats and the camels found plenty of water and freshly sprouted grass. All the village families rejoiced in the prosperity and blessing of the rain.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	dabeecadda	17	50
sheekadii-ayeeyo-xaliimo	Sheekadii Habeenkii ee Ayeeyo Xaliimo	Grandmother Xaliimo’s Bedtime Tale	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Habeenkii markii cashada la cunay, Ayeeyo Xaliimo waxay shidday faynuus iftiin diirran leh. Carruurtu waxay ku soo urureen ayeeyo agteeda iyagoo huwan go’yaal jilicsan. Ayeeyo waxay bilowday sheeko ku saabsan sidii xiddigaha cirku ugu iftiimi jireen socotada habeenkii. Codkeeda deggen wuxuu u ekaa neecawda habeenkii ee ruxaysa caleemaha geedka. Carruurtu waxay barteen magaca xiddigta Waaberi iyo sida loogu mahadceliyo nimcada nabadda. Intii aysan sheekadii dhammaan, carruurtii oo dhan waxay galeen hurdo macaan oo xasilloon.	At night after dinner was eaten, Grandmother Xaliimo lit a lantern with a warm glow. The children gathered beside their grandmother wrapped in soft blankets. Grandmother began a story about how the sky stars used to guide night travellers. Her calm voice sounded like the night breeze rustling the tree leaves. The children learned the name of the Morning Star and how to be thankful for the blessing of peace. Before the story even finished, all the children drifted into a sweet, peaceful sleep.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	habeenkii	18	50
safarkii-buurta-daallo	Safarkii Buurta Cagaaran ee Daallo	Journey to the Green Mountain of Daallo	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Saciid iyo walaashiis Nasteexo waxay subax hore u safreen buurta dheer ee Daallo. Marba marka ay buurta kor u sii fuulaan, hawadu waxay noqonaysay mid qabow oo udgoon. Waxay arkeen geedo dayib ah oo aad u dhaadheer iyo ceeryaamo cad oo laamaha dhex maraysa. Shimbir midabbo badan leh ayaa geedka dushiisa ka heestay cod macaan. Dusha sare ee buurta waxay ka eego-daawadeen dooxooyinka iyo badda fog. Saciid wuxuu buuggiisa xusuus-qorka ku sawiray geedaha iyo shimbiraha Daallo.	Saciid and his sister Nasteexo travelled early in the morning to the high mountain of Daallo. The higher they climbed up the mountain, the cooler and more fragrant the air became. They saw tall juniper trees and white mist weaving through the branches. A brightly coloured bird sang a sweet melody from the top of a tree. From the summit of the mountain they looked out across the valleys and the distant sea. Saciid sketched the trees and birds of Daallo in his notebook.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	tacabur	19	50
faraska-booddo	ubadkii Geela iyo Dooxada Nugaal	The Young Camels of the Nugaal Valley	Ages 6–8 • Da’da 6–8 sano	Level 2 — Akhriste Yar (Ages 6–8)	Dooxada ballaaran ee Nugaal waxay xilliga barwaaqada u egtahay roog cagaaran oo la fidiyay. Nirgaha yaryar ee geela ayaa subaxdii ku wada ordaya bannaanka xerada agteeda. Idil iyo walaalkeed waxay ka caawiyeen aabbahood in biyaha loo shubo xoolaha. Aabbe wuxuu qaaday hees-howleed dhaqameed oo lagu ammaanayo geela markii la waraabinayo. Idil waxay xifdisay miraha heesta, waxayna baratay magacyada geela. Fiidkii waxay wada cabbeen caano daray ah iyagoo ku faraxsan nolosha miyiga.	During the prosperous rainy season, the wide Nugaal valley looks like a spread-out green carpet. The young camel calves run playfully together in the open meadow near the enclosure in the morning. Idil and her brother helped their father pour water into the troughs for the animals. Father sang a traditional pastoral work song praising the camels as they were watered. Idil memorized the verses of the song and learned the traditional names of the camels. In the evening they drank fresh milk together, rejoicing in the pastoral life.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-2	dhaqanka	20	50
ceelkii-la-wadaagay	Ceelkii Nabadda iyo Wadaagga	The Well of Peace and Sharing	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Guga oo daahay awgiis, ceelka weyn ee Dooxada dhexe wuxuu noqday isha keliya ee biyaha laga helo. Subax kaliya ayaa laba kooxood oo xoolo-dhaqato ah isugu yimaadeen ceelka, mid walbana wuxuu rabay inuu hor waraabsado. Hanad oo ah wiil laba iyo toban jir ah oo caqli badan ayaa odayaasha weydiistay inuu fikrad soo jeediyo. "Haddii aan wada dhisno laba dar oo dhaadheer oo is-barbar yaal, oo aan wada dawlisanno biyaha, labada xero isku mar ayay cabbi karaan," ayuu yiri Hanad. Odayaashii waxay la dhaceen xigmadda wiilka yar, dhallinyaradiina si wada-jir ah ayay uga shaqeeyeen ceelka. Geelii iyo adhigii labada dhinacba si xasilloon ayay u cabbeen biyihii iyadoo aan muran dhicin. Maalintaas wixii ka dambeeyay, ceelkaas waxaa loo bixiyay "Ceelkii Nabadda iyo Wadaagga".	Because the spring rains were delayed, the great well in the central valley became the only source of water. On the same morning two groups of herders arrived at the well together, and each wanted to water their animals first. Hanad, a thoughtful twelve-year-old boy, respectfully asked the elders for permission to suggest an idea. "If we build two long troughs side by side and draw the water together, both herds can drink at the same time," said Hanad. The elders admired the young boy’s wisdom, and the youth worked together side by side at the well. The camels and flocks of both sides drank the water calmly without any dispute. From that day onward, the well was named "The Well of Peace and Sharing".	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	dhaqanka	21	65
runta-iyo-amaanada	Runta iyo Amaanada: Kiishkii Lacagta	Truth and Honesty: The Lost Purse	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Sagal oo dugsiga ka soorawaxday ayaa jidka suuqa agtiisa ku aragtay kiish yar oo maqaar ka samaysan. Markii ay furtay si ay u eegto cidda leh, waxay ku dhex aragtay lacag iyo warqad ay ku qoran tahay "Xaaji Maxamuud". In kasta oo ay gaajoonaysay oo suuqa macmacaan yaallay, Sagal waxay xusuusatay casharkii waalidkeed ee amaanada. Waxay u tagtay guddoomiyaha suuqa oo ay weydiisay halka uu ku yaallo dukaanka Xaaji Maxamuud. Xaaji Maxamuud oo murugaysan oo raadinaya lacagtii uu ku bixin lahaa deynta ayaa arkay Sagal oo u sidda kiishkii. Markii uu tiriyay lacagtii oo dhan oo aan hal shilin ka dhinayn, indhihiisa ilmo farxadeed ayaa ku soo istaagtay. Maamulaha dugsiga ayaa subaxdii xigtay Sagal ku abaalmariyay billadda daacadnimada iyo amaanada.	While walking home from school, Sagal noticed a small leather pouch near the market path. When she opened it to check who owned it, she saw money inside along with a note bearing the name "Xaaji Maxamuud". Although she was hungry and sweet treats were sold in the market, Sagal remembered her parents’ teaching about honesty. She went to the market elder and asked where Xaaji Maxamuud’s shop was located. Xaaji Maxamuud, who was worriedly searching for the money needed to pay his suppliers, saw Sagal bringing him the pouch. When he counted all the money and found not a single coin missing, tears of gratitude filled his eyes. The next morning the school principal honoured Sagal with a medal for honesty and trustworthiness.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	saaxiibtinimada	22	65
ilaaliyaha-dhirta-miyiga	Ilaaliyaha Dhirta Miyiga	Guardian of the Countryside Trees	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Cabdiraxmaan wuxuu dareemay in dooxadii tuuladooda ay dabayshu ciidda ka qaadayso ka dib markii geedo badan la jaray. Wuxuu macallinkiisa sayniska ka bartay in xididdada geeduhu ay qabtaan ciidda isla markaana soo jiitaan biyaha roobka. Jimcihii xigay, Cabdiraxmaan wuxuu la hadlay odayaasha iyo dhallinyarada tuulada isagoo sharxay khatarta nabaad-guurka. Tuulada oo dhan waxay ku heshiisay xeer cusub: in aan la jarin geed qoyan, qof walbana uu beero laba geed. Ardayda dugsiga waxay jiinka togagga ku beereen laba boqol oo geed oo quraac iyo gob ah. Laba xilli-roobaad ka dib, dooxadii waxay mar kale noqotay kayn cagaaran oo shimbiruhu ku hoydaan.	Cabdiraxmaan noticed that the wind was eroding the soil in their village valley after many trees had been cut down. He learned from his science teacher that tree roots hold the soil together and help absorb rainwater. The following Friday, Cabdiraxmaan spoke to the village elders and youth, explaining the danger of soil erosion. The entire village agreed on a new rule: never to cut a living tree, and for every person to plant two saplings. The school students planted two hundred acacia and Ziziphus trees along the banks of the seasonal streams. Two rainy seasons later, the valley once again became a lush green woodland where birds made their homes.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	dabeecadda	23	65
xiddig-iyaha-badmaaxa	Xiddig-Aqoonkii Yar ee Badmaaxa	The Young Star-Navigator of the Sea	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Nuur wuxuu awoowgiis oo ahaa naakhuude ruug-caddaa ah ka bartay magacyada xiddigaha iyo jihooyinka badda. Galab iyagoo badda ku maqan ayaa daruuro culus soo mareen, diiraddii yaraana way ka jabtay. Markii habeenkii dumay ee daruurihii kala baxeen, kalluumaysatadii waxay garan waayeen dhanka xeebtu ka xigto. Nuur ayaa kor u eegay cirka, wuxuuna isla markiiba gartay Xiddigta Jahada (Waqooyi) oo aan meesheeda ka dhaqaaqin. "Haddii Xiddigta Jahadu naga xigto midigta, xeebta Marka waxay naga xigtaa galbeedka tooska ah," ayuu yiri Nuur. Saacad ka dib, waxay meel fog ka arkeen iftiinka faynuusyada dekadda Marka oo soo dhawaynaya.	Nuur learned the names of the stars and the sea directions from his grandfather, a veteran sea captain. One afternoon while out at sea, heavy clouds rolled in and their small compass broke. When night fell and the clouds parted, the fishermen could not tell which direction led back to shore. Nuur looked up at the sky and immediately identified the North Star (Jahada), which remains fixed in place. "If the North Star is on our right side, the coast of Marka lies straight to the west," said Nuur. An hour later, they spotted in the distance the warm lantern lights of Marka harbour welcoming them home.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	tacabur	24	65
libaaxii-iyo-jiirkii-yaraa	Libaaxii Weynaa iyo Jiirkii Yaraa	The Great Lion and the Little Mouse	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Maalin kulul, libaax weyn oo ah boqorka kaynta ayaa hoos seexday geed quraac ah. Jiir yar oo cawska dhex ordaya ayaa si kama’ ah u dul maray cagta libaaxa, markaasuu libaaxii toosay. "I cafi, boqorow! Maalin uun waan kuu abaal-gudi doonaa," ayuu ku baryootamay jiirkii yaraa. Libaaxii wuu qoslay oo si naxariis leh ayuu u sii daayay jiirkii yaraa. Maalmo ka dib, libaaxii wuxuu ku dhacay shabaq xadhko adag ka samaysan oo ugaadhsato dhigtay. Jiirkii yaraa ayaa maqlay cida libaaxa, wuxuuna ku soo orday si uu ilkihiisa afka badan ugu gooyo xadhkaha shabaqa. Libaaxii oo xoroobay ayaa u mahadceliyay saaxiibkiisa yaraa, wuxuuna ogaaday in naxariistu aysan weligeed lumin.	On a warm day, a great lion, king of the woodland, slept beneath the shade of an acacia tree. A tiny mouse running through the grass accidentally ran across the lion’s paw, waking the lion up. "Forgive me, O King! One day I will repay your kindness," pleaded the little mouse. The lion chuckled and mercifully set the little mouse free. Days later, the lion became trapped in a net woven of thick ropes set by hunters. The little mouse heard the lion’s roar and ran over to gnaw through the net ropes with his sharp teeth. Freed at last, the lion thanked his tiny friend and realized that kindness is never lost.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	xayawaanka	25	65
tartankii-akhriska-dugsiga	Tartankii Akhriska iyo Maktabadda Dugsiga	The School Reading Contest and the Library	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Dugsiga Hoose iyo Dhexe ee Iftiin wuxuu ku dhawaaqay tartan weyn oo lagu tartamayo akhriska sheekooyinka Af-Soomaaliga. Deeqa oo ahayd gabadh aad u jecel akhriska waxay aragtay in qaar ka mid ah ardayda fasalkeedu ay ku adag yihiin erayada dhaadheer. Halkii ay keligeed is-diyaarin lahayd, Deeqa waxay aasaastay "Naadiga Akhriska Galabtii" ee maktabadda dugsiga. Maalin kasta waxay sabuuradda ku qori jireen shan eray oo cusub, wayna iska dhageysan jireen akhriska. Maalintii tartanka, fasalka Deeqa oo dhan wuxuu muujiyay akhris faseex ah iyo faham sare. Guddigii garsoorka waxay fasalka Deeqa gudoonsiiyeen koobka koowaad iyo konton buug oo cusub oo maktabadda lagu daro.	Iftiin Primary and Middle School announced a grand tournament for reading Somali stories. Deeqa, who loved reading deeply, noticed that some of her classmates struggled with longer words. Instead of preparing all alone, Deeqa founded the "Afternoon Reading Club" in the school library. Every day they wrote five new words on the chalkboard and listened to one another read aloud. On the day of the tournament, Deeqa’s entire class demonstrated fluent reading and deep comprehension. The judging panel awarded Deeqa’s class the first-place trophy and fifty new books for the school library.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	dugsiga	26	65
dhismaha-aqalka-soomaaliga	Farshaxanka iyo Dhismaha Aqalka Soomaaliga	The Craft and Building of the Somali Aqal	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Hibo waxay fasaxa dugsiga ku booqatay reerka ayeeyadeed oo deggen deegaan cagaaran oo miyi ah. Waxay aragtay dumarka reerka oo si xirfad leh uga shaqaynaya dhismaha aqal cusub oo qurux badan. Ayeeyadeed ayaa u sharxday sida dhigaha qalloocan iyo udubbada dhexe ay aqalka uga dhigaan mid u adkaysta dabaysha. Hibo waxay gacanteeda ku taabatay kebedda iyo dermada midabbada dabiiciga ah lagu xardhay. Gudaha aqalka wuxuu ahaa mid qabow marka qorraxdu kulushahay, habeenkiina diirran. Hibo waxay qortay warbixin cilmiyeed oo ay ardayda dugsigeeda ugu sharxayso injineernimada Aqalka Soomaaliga.	During the school holiday, Hibo visited her grandmother’s family living in a green pastoral settlement. She watched the women of the settlement skilfully constructing a beautiful new traditional home. Her grandmother explained how the curved arches and central pillars make the dome home resilient against strong winds. Hibo touched with her own hands the thick roof mats and sleeping mats decorated with natural geometric dyes. Inside, the aqal remained naturally cool when the sun was hot, and warm during the night. Hibo wrote a research report to explain to her school classmates the eco-friendly engineering of the Somali Aqal.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	dhaqanka	27	65
maroodigii-iyo-webiga-shabeelle	Maroodigii Da’da Weynaa iyo Webiga	The Elder Elephant and the River	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Tuulada Mahad waxay ku taal jiinka webiga Shabeelle, halkaas oo beeruhu ka baxaan. Xilligii abaarta, raxan maroodiyaal ah oo uu hoggaaminayo maroodi da’ weyn ayaa u soo dhaqaaqday dhanka webiga. Beeralaydii waxay ka walwaleen in maroodiyaashu ay kuumaraan dalagga galleyda iyo mooska. Mahad oo daraaseeyay dhaqanka maroodiga ayaa ogaaday in maroodiyaashu ay mar walba raacaan jidkii hore ee awoowayaashood. Tuuladu waxay banaysay marin ballaaran oo toos u taga biyaha webiga, waxayna geesaha beeraha ku xireen shinni-xanaano. Maroodiyaashii si nabad ah ayay webiga uga cabbeen iyagoo aan hal geed oo beer ah dhaawicin.	Mahad’s village lies along the bank of the Shabelle River, where lush farms grow. During the dry season, a herd of elephants led by an elder elephant moved toward the river. The farmers worried that the elephants might trample their crops of maize and bananas. Mahad, who had studied elephant behaviour, realized that elephants always follow their ancestral migration path. The village cleared a wide corridor leading straight to the river water and placed beehive fences along the farm borders. The elephants drank peacefully from the river without damaging a single farm plant.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	xayawaanka	28	65
nabadda-tuulada-barwaaqo	Buundadii Iskaashiga ee Tuulada Barwaaqo	The Bridge of Cooperation in Barwaaqo Village	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Tuulada Barwaaqo waxaa dhex mara tog weyn oo xilliga roobka biyo badan keena. Markii roobku da’o, carruurta yaryar way ku adkaan jirtay inay u tallaabaan dhanka dugsiga. Khaalid iyo Muna oo ah ardayda fasalka lixaad ayaa macallinkooda iyo waalidiinta u soobandhigay qorshe buundo lagu dhisayo. Qoys walba wuxuu keenay dhagaxaan siman, alwaax adag, iyo xadhko lagu xiro tiirarka. Saddex maalmood oo shaqo wada-jir ah ka dib, buundo adag oo leh biraha gacanta lagu qabsado ayaa la dhammaystiray. Carruurtii yaryarayd waxay buundada uga gudbeen farxad iyo ammaan iyagoo u socda dugsigooda.	Through Barwaaqo village runs a wide seasonal stream that fills with water during the rains. Whenever the rain fell, it became difficult for the younger children to cross over to the school side. Khaalid and Muna, sixth-grade students, presented to their teacher and parents a plan to build a footbridge. Every family contributed smooth stones, strong timber planks, and ropes to secure the railings. After three days of cooperative work, a sturdy bridge with safe handrails was completed. The young children crossed the bridge in joy and safety on their way to school.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	saaxiibtinimada	29	65
rijada-habeenka-curashada	Habeenka Curashada Sanadka iyo Riyada Mustaqbalka	New Year’s Eve and Dreams of the Future	Ages 9–12 • Da’da 9–12 sano	Level 3 — Akhriste Horumarsan (Ages 9–12)	Habeen xasilloon oo bil cusub iyo sanad cusub bilaabanayaan, qoyska Yasmiin waxay ku kulmeen barxadda guriga. Faynuus iftiin diirran leh ayaa dhex yaallay dermada, cirkana waxaa ka muuqday dayax iyo xiddigo dhalaalaya. Qof walba wuxuu ka sheekeeyay sheekadii ugu fiicnayd ee uu akhriyay sanadkii dhammaaday iyo casharkii uu ka bartay. Yasmiin waxay sheegtay inay baratay boqol eray oo cusub oo Af-Soomaali ah iyo sida loo qoro sheekooyin gaagaaban. Aabbe iyo Hooyo waxay carruurta siiyeen buugaag cusub oo ay ku qortaan riyooyinka iyo yoolalka sanadka cusub. Yasmiin waxay bogga koowaad ku qortay: "Sanadkan waxaan akhrin doonaa soddon sheeko, waxaana caawin doonaa carruurta yaryar." Habeenkaasi wuxuu ku dhammaaday duco, rajo wanaagsan, iyo hurdo xasilloon.	On a calm evening marking the start of a new month and a new year, Yasmiin’s family gathered in the courtyard. A warm lantern stood in the centre of the woven mat, and a bright moon and stars shone in the sky. Everyone shared the favourite story they had read during the past year and the lesson they had learned from it. Yasmiin shared that she had learned a hundred new Somali words and how to write short stories of her own. Father and Mother gifted the children new notebooks in which to write their dreams and goals for the new year. On the first page Yasmiin wrote: "This year I will read thirty stories, and I will help younger children learn to read." That evening concluded with blessings, bright hope, and peaceful sleep.	so	["so","en"]	Folio Horn of Africa Children’s Literacy Collection (Original Educational Text)	Bahda Waxbarashada Folio (Folio Somali Literacy Editorial Board)	Folio Digital Library — Open Educational Children’s Series	Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)	published_text_pending_audio	2026-11-03T10:47:10.999Z	level-3	habeenkii	30	70
